{
 "meta": {
  "district": "olympic-park",
  "source": "hand-made inside (not to scale), on the real outline at 1/4: Olympic Park in Songpa-gu, built for the 1988 Seoul Olympics. Olympic-ro (west side, north-north-east from Mongchontoseong Station) and Wiryeseong-daero (south side) follow OpenStreetMap at 1/4 (© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL); the north and east edges follow Seongnaecheon. Estimated where the OSM export ends: Wiryeseong-daero east of Bangi-dong runs straight on, and the east edge between the stream and Wiryeseong-daero is a straight line. Inside, laid out for play rather than the real spots (Yozi 2026-11-11): everything to do sits round the paved Peace Plaza, a short walk from the station: the World Peace Gate (stylised), the pungmul troupe, the pool hall, the skate park and basketball court, the lone tree on its own lawn and the pond. Lawns for picnics, a few grass beds on the plaza, cherry trees along the loop walk and a wood on the east side; the skate park, the pool hall and the basketball court are game additions. Placed by its anchor, the World Peace Gate (region.json)."
 },
